WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.609 --> 00:00:04.109
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.077
- One of the biggest problems I ran into

00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:14.033
and this is really embarrassing
to say on camera, was.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.270
Its officially official,
four weeks of going vegan

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.340
are in the books, and I'm
so happy about my goal.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.380
I have to thank you
guys for challenging me

00:00:29.205 --> 00:00:31.235
Just to clarify, there are many reasons

00:00:31.235 --> 00:00:33.225
why people follow a vegan diet.

00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:35.245
Moral, ethical, environmental,

00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:37.075
but information I'm gonna cover here,

00:00:37.075 --> 00:00:39.975
is only what's related
to nutrition, and health.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:42.175
If you want me to talk
about those other concepts

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.565
I'm happy to do so, drop me a line below

00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:47.293
and it will make a dedicated
vegan video to just that.

00:00:47.293 --> 00:00:50.285
(playful music)

00:00:50.285 --> 00:00:53.545
A vegan diet can be a very healthy diet.

00:00:53.545 --> 00:00:56.675
Whether you're young,
old, somewhere in between

00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:59.555
pregnant, nonpregnant,
breastfeeding, not breastfeeding,

00:00:59.555 --> 00:01:02.465
basically it's applicable
to all life stages.

00:01:02.465 --> 00:01:04.455
The reason I put that word canon there,

00:01:04.455 --> 00:01:07.285
you can follow a vegan
diet, eat vegan burgers

00:01:07.285 --> 00:01:09.665
with sugary sodas, with gummy candies,

00:01:09.665 --> 00:01:12.635
still be vegan, and that's
not really healthy, right?

00:01:12.635 --> 00:01:17.035
And I have to say, it's not the
only healthy diet out there.

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:19.575
Some of the loudest voices
in the vegan community

00:01:19.575 --> 00:01:23.225
are quick to say that veganism
is the only healthy option

00:01:23.225 --> 00:01:24.145
that's not the case,

00:01:24.145 --> 00:01:26.585
there are several other
healthy diets out there,

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:28.105
for example The Mediterranean diet

00:01:28.105 --> 00:01:30.735
that I'm personally a fan
of, that are just as healthy,

00:01:30.735 --> 00:01:32.597
if not, healthier than the vegan diet.

00:01:32.597 --> 00:01:35.565
(playful music)

00:01:35.565 --> 00:01:37.155
I have to be honest and admit that

00:01:37.155 --> 00:01:40.825
I don't generally recommend
vegan as my first option.

00:01:40.825 --> 00:01:42.665
I do know that its a restrictive diet,

00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:45.105
and we know restrictive diets
have high failure rates.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.365
Plus, the benefits of a vegan
diet, aren't that much better

00:01:48.365 --> 00:01:49.715
than some of the other alternatives

00:01:49.715 --> 00:01:50.745
that are simpler to follow.

00:01:50.745 --> 00:01:51.885
When I recommend a diet,

00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:54.075
I'm trying to create the healthiest diet,

00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:56.415
but also one that's
feasible and achievable

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:59.125
for my patients to face
without disrupting their lives.

00:01:59.125 --> 00:02:01.355
On the other hand, if one
of my patients comes in

00:02:01.355 --> 00:02:03.375
and wants to follow a vegan diet,

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.115
I'm totally in support of that,

00:02:05.115 --> 00:02:06.335
I just have to make sure that

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:08.345
they're adequately planning their meals,

00:02:08.345 --> 00:02:10.155
their supplementing when need be,

00:02:10.155 --> 00:02:11.585
checking their blood tests,

00:02:11.585 --> 00:02:13.885
and ideally having some
guidance either from myself

00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:15.165
or a nutritionist.

00:02:15.165 --> 00:02:18.125
(playful music)

00:02:18.125 --> 00:02:20.295
The research behind health benefits

00:02:20.295 --> 00:02:24.255
of following a vegan diet are
substantial, and high quality.

00:02:24.255 --> 00:02:26.225
If you're following standard American diet

00:02:26.225 --> 00:02:28.015
and then switch over to a vegan diet,

00:02:28.015 --> 00:02:30.015
you're gonna see improvement
and chronic diseases

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:33.005
like diabetes, heart disease, strokes,

00:02:33.005 --> 00:02:35.515
even an extension of life in some cases.

00:02:35.515 --> 00:02:37.465
And what's most interesting is when we add

00:02:37.465 --> 00:02:39.725
some animal product into the mix,

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:41.875
those outcomes still hold true.

00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:43.705
That's why what I
recommend to my patients,

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:45.305
is a plant focused diet.

00:02:45.305 --> 00:02:46.835
Meaning that they should get the majority

00:02:46.835 --> 00:02:48.715
of their calories from plants.

00:02:48.715 --> 00:02:53.565
Fruits, vegetables, legumes,
nuts, seeds, healthy fats,

00:02:53.565 --> 00:02:55.815
and a modern amount of poultry and fish,

00:02:55.815 --> 00:02:57.335
with a minimal amount of red meat.

00:02:57.335 --> 00:02:59.455
In fact, that's the diet I follow,

00:02:59.455 --> 00:03:00.955
and recommend to my own family.

00:03:00.955 --> 00:03:03.785
The field of nutrition
research has ever changing

00:03:03.785 --> 00:03:06.595
and as we get more information,
more quality studies,

00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:08.425
we, doctors and nutritionists alike

00:03:08.425 --> 00:03:10.615
are gonna be able to give
better recommendations

00:03:10.615 --> 00:03:13.085
when it comes to a vegan
diet, a plant focused diet.

00:03:13.085 --> 00:03:15.145
All of this is susceptible to change,

00:03:15.145 --> 00:03:17.125
but its important that we
make the best decisions

00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:19.075
with the knowledge that we have on hand.

00:03:19.075 --> 00:03:21.495
The one thing that I can
say with 100% certainty

00:03:21.495 --> 00:03:25.357
is there's no such thing as
a miracle diet for everybody.

00:03:25.357 --> 00:03:28.445
(playful music)

00:03:28.445 --> 00:03:30.135
On day one, I was excited,

00:03:30.135 --> 00:03:31.625
I was like, if I could tackle keto,

00:03:33.029 --> 00:03:36.969
The first point at which
I had a little hesitation,

00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:40.168
was when I ordered my
first, at-home delivery.

00:03:40.168 --> 00:03:43.001
(deep bass music)

00:03:45.089 --> 00:03:48.799
Buffalo cauliflower bites,

00:03:48.799 --> 00:03:53.799
with some kind of not real
mayo, and this is a wrap,

00:03:55.339 --> 00:03:59.782
with vegan cheese, and unchicken.

00:04:01.013 --> 00:04:02.949
What is unchicken?

00:04:02.949 --> 00:04:05.079
I was having second thoughts,

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:06.159
and that's not like me.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:07.629
If I set a goal for myself,

00:04:07.629 --> 00:04:10.589
I'm gonna do everything in
my power to meet that goal.

00:04:10.589 --> 00:04:13.319
But for some reason when
sticking into this vegan diet,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.099
I was concerned about so many things.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:16.969
The following week, I was leaving to MIT

00:04:16.969 --> 00:04:18.339
for the leadership conference,

00:04:18.339 --> 00:04:20.709
I was worried if they're gonna
have vegan options available

00:04:20.709 --> 00:04:23.619
for me, I was then traveling
to Miami for a few days,

00:04:23.619 --> 00:04:25.999
all these worries started
bubbling in my head

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.439
and I was really wondering,

00:04:27.439 --> 00:04:30.299
can I stick to vegan this entire month?

00:04:30.299 --> 00:04:31.639
Why should I do vegan?

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:32.909
- Because it's more
healthier for you, boo.

00:04:32.909 --> 00:04:33.819
- You think so?
- Yes.

00:04:33.819 --> 00:04:35.709
- But 30 days' a long time.

00:04:35.709 --> 00:04:38.504
- Just do it!

00:04:38.504 --> 00:04:41.189
(playful music)

00:04:41.189 --> 00:04:43.509
- One of the first
obstacles I ran into on the

00:04:43.509 --> 00:04:46.619
vegan diet was undereating calories.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.919
Now, I'm partially to blame
here, 'cause I didn't prep well

00:04:49.919 --> 00:04:52.096
and even at the opening
of this video, I said,

00:04:52.096 --> 00:04:54.339
"The healthy way to follow a vegan diet,

00:04:54.339 --> 00:04:56.299
is to adequately plan your meals."

00:04:56.299 --> 00:04:58.029
For the first two weeks,
I have to be honest,

00:04:58.029 --> 00:04:59.359
I didn't have much of an appetite.

00:04:59.359 --> 00:05:02.329
I'm not a huge fan of
just eating vegetables,

00:05:02.329 --> 00:05:03.689
and rice, and beans.

00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:05.549
So, I didn't have tremendous portions,

00:05:05.549 --> 00:05:08.099
and because of that,
I was calorie deficit,

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:09.749
I actually noticed some weight loss.

00:05:09.749 --> 00:05:12.519
What helped me tremendously to
make up those calorie deficit

00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:15.329
is eating some of these
snacks that Thrive sent over.

00:05:15.329 --> 00:05:18.009
If I didn't have these snacks,
I'd be undereating calories

00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:19.379
the majority of the time.

00:05:19.379 --> 00:05:22.449
Long days in the hospital,
but I got my Simple Mills.

00:05:22.449 --> 00:05:26.566
These crackers, gave me
through some rough, rough days.

00:05:26.566 --> 00:05:29.745
(playful music)

00:05:29.745 --> 00:05:31.566
One of the biggest problems I ran into,

00:05:31.566 --> 00:05:34.489
and this is really
embarrassing to say on camera.

00:05:34.489 --> 00:05:37.219
The whole plane ride I'm
sitting next to a doctor

00:05:37.219 --> 00:05:39.359
my stomach is going (gurgles)

00:05:39.359 --> 00:05:41.959
had to ask him to stand
up like three, four times.

00:05:41.959 --> 00:05:45.369
From day one, up until
the last day of the diet,

00:05:45.369 --> 00:05:48.139
I was having tremendous gas and bloating,

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:49.509
it's so embarrassing to say.

00:05:49.509 --> 00:05:52.389
I mean think about this, I fly on planes,

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:54.969
I interact with patients
for long periods of time,

00:05:54.969 --> 00:05:56.689
I sit in conferences,

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.669
I can't just be sitting
there with flatulent.

00:06:00.669 --> 00:06:03.009
I did try and isolate some ingredients

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:04.599
to see which ones were causing

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:06.929
this gas and bloating combination for me,

00:06:06.929 --> 00:06:08.399
but I couldn't find out what it was.

00:06:08.399 --> 00:06:09.639
I normally eat brown rice,

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:12.439
I normally eat vegetables,
and fruits, and beans,

00:06:12.439 --> 00:06:14.789
I expect them to go away after four weeks,

00:06:14.789 --> 00:06:16.479
but no, they stuck around.

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:17.819
I would have to say that the vegan diet

00:06:17.819 --> 00:06:20.009
probably won't work for me long-term.

00:06:20.009 --> 00:06:23.439
I just can't sit there with
my stomach going (gurgles)

00:06:23.439 --> 00:06:26.659
and me wanting to pass
gas the entire time.

00:06:26.659 --> 00:06:27.984
God, that's embarrassing.

00:06:27.984 --> 00:06:30.852
(playful music)

00:06:30.852 --> 00:06:34.599
What I didn't know about veganism
is that there are a ton of

00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:36.249
up incoming options,

00:06:36.249 --> 00:06:38.969
for those who aren't used to eating vegan.

00:06:38.969 --> 00:06:42.559
There are specialty restaurants
that just offer vegan foods

00:06:42.559 --> 00:06:44.189
with no animal products

00:06:44.189 --> 00:06:46.539
that remind you of foods
that you may have eaten

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.989
when you ate animal products,

00:06:47.989 --> 00:06:49.379
and I thought that was really cool.

00:06:49.379 --> 00:06:51.999
On top of that, a lot of these restaurants

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:54.429
and even some of the
products I got from Thrive

00:06:54.429 --> 00:06:58.169
tasted delicious, because of the sauces.

00:06:58.169 --> 00:07:00.429
Vegan sauces are on point.

00:07:00.429 --> 00:07:02.439
I'm loving these blue chips,

00:07:02.439 --> 00:07:04.349
but without some like sauce

00:07:04.349 --> 00:07:06.799
like I'm really digging
this primal kitchen,

00:07:06.799 --> 00:07:08.392
classic barbecue sauce.

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:11.080
These chips just aren't cutting it.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.929
(playful music)

00:07:13.929 --> 00:07:15.979
I've talked about on this channel

00:07:15.979 --> 00:07:17.449
of decision fatigue.

00:07:17.449 --> 00:07:19.689
Because you're constantly making decisions

00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:21.589
and you're using your willpower,

00:07:21.589 --> 00:07:23.809
its actually a finite resource.

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:26.149
What I noticed while I was
following the vegan diet

00:07:26.149 --> 00:07:29.709
was that, I lost the
drive to go to the gym.

00:07:29.709 --> 00:07:31.819
My work ethic actually suffered,

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:34.969
because I was putting
such a strong emphasis

00:07:34.969 --> 00:07:38.449
on sticking to vegan, when
there were so many temptations

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:39.839
and there were things I wanted to eat.

00:07:39.839 --> 00:07:42.139
I didn't want to hop on my
spin bike in my bedroom,

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:44.019
I didn't want to go to
the gym with my friends.

00:07:44.019 --> 00:07:46.349
This is really unlike
me, and it's an obstacle

00:07:46.349 --> 00:07:48.159
I didn't actually expect to face.

00:07:48.159 --> 00:07:50.349
When I went to the gym, I lifted fine,

00:07:50.349 --> 00:07:52.579
getting to the gym was
the actual struggle.

00:07:52.579 --> 00:07:55.459
(playful music)

00:07:55.459 --> 00:07:58.229
At the time I least expected it

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:01.535
disaster struck, I got sick.

00:08:01.535 --> 00:08:03.479
(coughs)

00:08:03.479 --> 00:08:05.799
I started coughing, I got a sore throat,

00:08:05.799 --> 00:08:07.089
I got a low-grade fever.

00:08:07.089 --> 00:08:10.209
I went to see the doctor,
I weighed the pros and cons

00:08:10.209 --> 00:08:13.379
of starting antibiotics,
of stopping the vegan diet.

00:08:13.379 --> 00:08:15.599
I decided to stick with
conservative treatment

00:08:15.599 --> 00:08:17.019
and treat it like a viral illness.

00:08:17.019 --> 00:08:19.949
One of my favorite hacks
to treat viral illnesses,

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:21.939
actually, symptoms of the viral illnesses,

00:08:21.939 --> 00:08:24.554
is green tea with manuka honey.

00:08:24.554 --> 00:08:25.387
(gasps)

00:08:25.387 --> 00:08:26.459
- [Woman] Patrol members be advised.

00:08:26.459 --> 00:08:28.619
- Freeze, vegan police, vegan police.

00:08:28.619 --> 00:08:32.309
- Apparently, honey is not vegan, what?

00:08:32.309 --> 00:08:34.959
I guess honey is an animal product,

00:08:34.959 --> 00:08:38.209
but man, I didn't force
the bees to make the honey,

00:08:38.209 --> 00:08:39.589
they make it on their own.

00:08:39.589 --> 00:08:42.629
We didn't have to milk them for it, wait.

00:08:42.629 --> 00:08:45.249
If you wanted to disqualify
my four week vegan challenge

00:08:45.249 --> 00:08:47.893
because I ate honey, so be it.

00:08:47.893 --> 00:08:50.909
(playful music)

00:08:50.909 --> 00:08:53.029
I gotta say, at this point, I was rolling,

00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:55.139
I was starting getting
into the vegan vibe,

00:08:55.139 --> 00:08:57.119
I was trying out new restaurants,

00:08:57.119 --> 00:08:58.939
I was sampling all the delicious foods

00:08:58.939 --> 00:09:00.129
that I got from Thrive,

00:09:00.129 --> 00:09:02.749
and I was excited, I was getting
close to the finish line.

00:09:02.749 --> 00:09:05.849
But I will say one of the hardest
things with the vegan diet

00:09:05.849 --> 00:09:07.119
is peer pressure.

00:09:07.119 --> 00:09:09.459
I mean, when I went out
to eat with my friends,

00:09:09.459 --> 00:09:11.949
they were annoyed to say the least

00:09:11.949 --> 00:09:13.339
that we had to choose the restaurant

00:09:13.339 --> 00:09:15.059
based on my eating preferences.

00:09:15.059 --> 00:09:19.789
I did do a decent job at trying
to pick out vegan options

00:09:19.789 --> 00:09:21.569
in not so vegan places.

00:09:21.569 --> 00:09:23.122
Look at this dedication.

00:09:24.899 --> 00:09:27.049
Greek salad, no feta,

00:09:27.049 --> 00:09:29.039
asparagus, fries.
- [Woman] Oh wait for me.

00:09:29.039 --> 00:09:30.539
- While I got this next to me,

00:09:31.849 --> 00:09:35.340
while Keith is eating this.
- [Keith] Mm.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.586
- [Woman] And I'm eating octopus

00:09:36.586 --> 00:09:37.661
- [Mike] ... is eating that, octopus.

00:09:37.661 --> 00:09:38.929
(laughter)

00:09:38.929 --> 00:09:40.293
What are you eating?

00:09:40.293 --> 00:09:41.126
- Fish.

00:09:42.259 --> 00:09:43.876
- The vegan struggle's real.

00:09:43.876 --> 00:09:46.209
(playful music)

00:09:46.209 --> 00:09:48.259
I wanna say I was really proud of myself,

00:09:48.259 --> 00:09:49.589
and it's nice every now and then

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.169
to take a challenge like this,

00:09:51.169 --> 00:09:52.859
and learn something new about yourself,

00:09:52.859 --> 00:09:54.929
in fact, I want to tell you five things

00:09:54.929 --> 00:09:56.909
that I learned not only
about the vegan diet,

00:09:56.909 --> 00:09:58.999
but also about myself during this process.

00:09:58.999 --> 00:10:03.289
One, when I didn't plan
well, I ate very unhealthy.

00:10:03.289 --> 00:10:05.459
When I was at MIT for breakfast,

00:10:05.459 --> 00:10:08.619
I ate Cinnamon Toast Crunch
with almond milk, and a banana

00:10:08.619 --> 00:10:11.909
every morning, that's not
healthy even though it's vegan.

00:10:11.909 --> 00:10:14.059
Two, I didn't notice a major change

00:10:14.059 --> 00:10:15.929
in my energy level like I thought I would.

00:10:15.929 --> 00:10:18.609
I mean maybe I had a slightly
decreased energy level

00:10:18.609 --> 00:10:20.329
but we have to remember that I was sick,

00:10:20.329 --> 00:10:22.259
and in the beginning I
was undereating calories

00:10:22.259 --> 00:10:24.839
so I don't feel its fair
to blame vegan for that.

00:10:24.839 --> 00:10:28.279
Three, surprisingly I
didn't weaker on vegan,

00:10:28.279 --> 00:10:30.629
I was lifting strong and I felt good.

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:33.439
But what did suffer,
was getting to the gym.

00:10:33.439 --> 00:10:36.039
I really noticed a lack of willpower

00:10:36.039 --> 00:10:38.559
when I was following
this restrictive diet.

00:10:38.559 --> 00:10:40.559
Four, when it comes to my body

00:10:40.559 --> 00:10:44.349
I lost three pounds, I dropped
from 203, to 200 pounds

00:10:44.349 --> 00:10:45.729
so there was some weight loss,

00:10:45.729 --> 00:10:47.349
probably from undereating calories.

00:10:47.349 --> 00:10:50.189
But, despite losing weight,
I didn't feel as lean.

00:10:50.189 --> 00:10:52.889
I mean all those sauces,
all the rice that I ate,

00:10:52.889 --> 00:10:55.289
pasta, that contributed to the carb load

00:10:55.289 --> 00:10:58.109
and probably made me feel a
little bit pudgier than usual.

00:10:58.109 --> 00:11:00.399
Five, this is the big one.

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:03.239
The real difficulty was my GI system,

00:11:03.239 --> 00:11:04.489
I mean it was a mess.

00:11:04.489 --> 00:11:07.387
The amount of gas, and
flatulence, and bloating got a,

00:11:07.387 --> 00:11:10.259
it's like gross to even talk
about, but it was really bad.

00:11:10.259 --> 00:11:12.429
If you have that with any diet,

00:11:12.429 --> 00:11:13.869
there's no way you're sticking with it.

00:11:13.869 --> 00:11:15.559
And I tried taking some over-the-counter

00:11:15.559 --> 00:11:16.439
supplements for this.

00:11:16.439 --> 00:11:17.756
It did absolutely nothing.

00:11:17.756 --> 00:11:20.789
(playful music)

00:11:20.789 --> 00:11:23.829
If you're curious or interested
in starting a vegan diet,

00:11:23.829 --> 00:11:25.719
I don't want to dissuade you, in fact,

00:11:25.719 --> 00:11:26.999
I want to encourage you.

00:11:26.999 --> 00:11:30.319
Go talk to a dietician,
nutritionist, physician,

00:11:30.319 --> 00:11:32.859
someone who is well-versed
with vegan diets

00:11:32.859 --> 00:11:36.039
that way you could do it
the healthy, happy, safe way

00:11:36.039 --> 00:11:38.059
without hurting yourself in the process.

00:11:38.059 --> 00:11:41.019
And please, reduce the
amount of refined carbs and

00:11:41.019 --> 00:11:42.559
processed foods that you're eating

00:11:42.559 --> 00:11:44.489
because as more research comes out,

00:11:44.489 --> 00:11:46.389
that's the stuff that causes diseases

00:11:46.389 --> 00:11:47.709
and shortens your lifespan.

00:11:47.709 --> 00:11:49.959
Now, if you want to check
out a really cool playlist,

00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:53.859
check out my nutrition playlist
right here for some goodies.

00:11:53.859 --> 00:11:56.692
Click here, and stay happy, and healthy.

00:11:56.692 --> 00:11:59.275
(upbeat music)

